        "username": "Arthur_Aihaken",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/arthur_aihaken/{size}/504104_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-09-05T09:05:31.966Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’m fine with multiboxing the way it is. You know how much content I lose to multiboxers? Almost zero (and some might argue that mining isn’t a “real” activity anyway). For most players running more than a handful of accounts isn’t very practical or easy to manage anyway.</p>\n<p>I’d also put forward the argument that GPUs and memory are kind of cost-prohibitive at this point in time anyway.</p>",
