        "id": 2922835,
        "name": "Princess Rose Ivory",
        "username": "Princess_Rose_Ivory",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/princess_rose_ivory/{size}/433985_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-09-05T11:41:40.041Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Seems like ages ago, I played a Chinese MMORPG titled <em>Jade Dynasty.</em> I didn’t need to play it for very long, it allowed botting – not by 3rd party software – the botting was built into the game. The Esper system allowed you to set up automated combat and skilling.  There was an AFK feature called “meditation” where your character did nothing and gained experience.  I got bored and quit playing.</p>\n<p>Suggesting to remove multi-boxing from this game is pointless. Fenris makes their income from omega accounts. What better way to sell multiple omega accounts, than to allow multi-boxing.  You probably stand a better chance to convince them to sell a built in botting system to players or maybe God Mode. As long as Fenris can make revenues from that system.</p>\n<p>My point is when there is no challenge, there is no game.</p>\n<p>Have fun!</p>",
